<title>USA: JFK air cargo up 2pct in Jan-April 1997.</title>
<headline>JFK air cargo up 2pct in Jan-April 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York's JFK airport handled 528,453 tonnes of airfreight in January-April, a rise of two percent over the 518,324 tonnes moved in same 1996 period, a Port Authority of New York and New Jersey spokesman said.</p>
<p>Newark Airport handled a total of 329,567 tonnes in January-April, up 7.7 percent on the 305,932 tonnes moved in 1996, he added.</p>
<p>In April JFK moved 135,035 tonnes against 135,184 in the same 1996 month while Newark's tonnages rose to 87,058 tonnes from 77,848 tonnes. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
